  <page_number>152</page_number>
  <running_head>ABRA. SACRIFICANS.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>V</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Fertilis charas calefacta fruges:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Explicet ustas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Vt sua Autumno reduente poma</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Colligant lati patulis coloni</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Arborum ramis, grauidisque amœnas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Vitibus Suas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Et diem iusto properum labori</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Destinans, grata sice reddit umbras</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Noctis, &amp; fessos hominum sopore</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Recreat artus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Mox pluens pingui rigat imbre campos,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Mox fugans nubes, madidosque ventos,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Stridulis sudi Borea serenat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Flatibus auras.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Et maris frenat rabidos tumultus:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Nec suas ultra patitur vagari</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Frouidus metas refluo furentes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Æquore fluctus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Sola te quondam bonitas fauere</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>I-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>mpulit nobis, meritoque nullo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Excitus cunctis pautidos periclis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Liberas funima dominator arcis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <i>Et locis tractos quibus execranda</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Turpibus placant simulachra vana</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" para="true">
      <i>Ritibus gentes, regis: atque certos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Tramites monstras, facilemque acerbis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28" para="true">
      <i>Exitum rebus. Duce te per urbes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" para="true">
      <i>Viximus tuti Pharias, cruenta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30" para="true">
      <i>Quum fames quondam Chananaea rura</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Show-through from the reverse page appears across the right side of the text; not transcribed. Some words in the verse are doubtfully read (e.g. "Fertilis", "Explicet ustas", "Sice", "Sola", "Excitus", "Liberas funima", "Frouidus"); these may be misprints or scan damage. The initial letters of several lines are unclear in the scan, and the long-s forms have been normalised to s.</notes>
